Changelog: 20-11-2026 18:49:20

Added. The window's new order (owner, 20-11-2026: shadPS4 Manager's design in every manager). The header's pills are
the Vita3K version, Vita3K Install, Vita3K Uninstall and Refresh. The row under them is Games Install, Games
Uninstall, Available in Steam and Play time. Games Uninstall is new: it is what the Remove game… button under the
table did, and that button went. The Your games box went. Under the pills are two columns: the three state lines,
each name with a colon (Vita3K:, Firmware:, Game folder:), and beside them Installed version:, the Vita3K version in
use. The tabs are Your games, Start game, Memory cards, Settings, View logs (it was Log) and Clear logs.

Added. A check for a game that is in Steam more than once. The app says which games and how often, the game's In
Steam box says it in its tooltip, and Update Steam lights and leaves one shortcut of each, with the latest play
time; its question says how many double shortcuts go.

Fixed. The chosen row of a table is 30 % blue, with the theme's text color: filled with the header's blue, a chosen
first row could hardly be told from the header above it.

Fixed. Start game with Steam closed started Steam and never the game, while the line said "Steam starts" (seen in
shadPS4 Manager on the board, 20-11-2026). The app now starts Steam first, waits until it takes commands, then gives
it the game's address, again when the game does not come up (core's play). The line says the game runs only once
Vita3K does, and says when Steam did not start it. While Vita3K runs already, Start game starts no second one.

Fixed. A shortcut whose fields Steam wrote in lower case (exe, launchoptions) was not recognized as the app's, so
Update Steam added the game a second time. They are read whatever their case now.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 13:11:18

Release 1.5.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 03:39:29

Added. The version manager (owner, 20-11-2026: as shadPS4's own launcher has one; core's builds). The version box in
the header is a pill: its menu lists the Vita3K builds installed and puts another in use, and Manage versions… opens
the version manager, which downloads the builds from GitHub, checked against the SHA-256 GitHub publishes, adds a
custom AppImage, puts a build in use and deletes one. Builds stay side by side: Install no longer deletes the others,
and puts the build this version was tried with back in use, without a download when it is still there. Uninstall
removes every build. A build other than the tested one is said to be not tried on the board.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 02:49:29

Release 1.4.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 02:18:33

Added. The app installs Vita3K build 4377 (was 4269; action list, 20-11-2026): emulator.py pins build 4377 (0.2.1,
commit 685b80a6), the SHA-256 GitHub publishes for its AppImage (de1ddd4b…9db2) and its size. Checked in Vita3K's
source between the two builds (108 changes): the command line the app uses (--firmware, --pkg, --zrif, -r) and the
config.yml keys it sets are unchanged.

